**curve.cpp maps, validates, and evaluates aim response curves.**

## Interface

`to_string(curve_kind k) noexcept -> const char*` returns `"linear"`/`"power"`; unknown kinds fall back to `"linear"`.

`validate(const response_curve& c, string& why) noexcept -> bool` rejects power curves unless `exponent` is finite and `> 0.0f`, setting `"power curve exponent must be finite and greater than zero"`.

`evaluate(const response_curve& c, float t) noexcept -> float` clamps `t` to `[0.0f, 1.0f]`, then applies identity or `std::pow(t, c.exponent)`.

## Dependencies

`std::isfinite`, `std::clamp`, and `std::pow` implement validation and evaluation.